                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued October 4 at 7:50PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "Areas of locally dense fog will persist along portions of the\nGlenn and Richardson Highways, especially from Glennallen west to\nMendeltna, this evening through early Monday morning.\n\nPeriods of a wintry mix of precipitation are also expected across\nthe Copper River Basin through Monday morning. With temperatures\naround freezing for most locations, any precipitation may fall as\na mix of rain, snow, and freezing drizzle. Little to no\nsignificant snow and ice accumulation is expected. However, the\ncombination of falling precipitation and temperatures around\nfreezing may result in slippery road conditions and patchy black\nice. The precipitation and fog is expected to taper off by early\nto mid Monday morning.\n\nMotorists are urged to slow down and use caution while traveling.\nFor the latest road conditions call 5 1 1 or visit\n511.alaska.gov.",
